id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Food, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"s688oKDwUayG5rjHbPwK7w","review_id":"CNez9H-sGdltLADPffpEFA","date":"2015-11-20T13:58:09","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.94034743309021,"text_excerpt":"Checked out Two Tony's for the first time on a Friday night, the night before Halloween. The restaurant had a good crowd, not full, but I'll attribute that to Halloween being moved up this year. Our server was friendly, seemed like a lady who had been working there awhile. I started with the soup of the day, a corn and red bell pepper bisque, really tasty. Also ordered was the House Italian Salad...if you like olive salad, get this! One of the best salads with a heaping helping of olive salad on top. I went with the Lasagna, really nice. It had a great red sauce, sweet, which I prefer. The Italian Sausage inside really upped the flavor. The Veal Parm was another entree enjoyed. Good porti..."},{"business_id":"s688oKDwUayG5rjHbPwK7w","review_id":"1fDou3lLXGJIk5WeMAMmLA","date":"2020-06-11T04:21:12","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9285459518432617,"text_excerpt":"A friend and I came to Two Tony's for dinner and it was excellent. We had the fried calamari which was superb along with the Italian salad that was filled with antipasto and a great dressing. When the entrees came they were surprisingly smaller than what you would get at most Italian joints around town but we didn't need a big entree since we had apps. My friend had the meatballs which were so tender and delicious they fell apart when your fork touched them. I had the veal parm which was again excellent. Only negative was we didn't get our garlic bread until after we ate our entree for some reason. They didn't take it off the bill so we at it in place of dessert and it was also excellent."},{"business_id":"s688oKDwUayG5rjHbPwK7w","review_id":"4ZbiK3NIldCKBqW0CTXRzg","date":"2019-06-22T18:22:19","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9264499545097351,"text_excerpt":"After a lot of back and forth on deciding where to go eat, my mom recommended that we check out Two Tony's. I had been in this building many years ago when it was a different restaurant. I have a fond memory of watching a 7 overtime game with my grandfather when I had been in this building before. So it was fun to reminisce that experience. The first take away I had when we first got there was that it was good for kids. They had high chairs readily available and a separate kids menu that we could quickly decide on... which is very handy when you have two hungry two year olds. The adults at the table had eaten lunch pretty late in the day so none of us were particularly hungry. So we decid..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"s688oKDwUayG5rjHbPwK7w","photo_id":"QyQuKYJD4hag5L_0YEgMBg","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/QyQuKYJD4hag5L_0YEgMBg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.857876181602478},{"business_id":"s688oKDwUay